#X obj 673 11 env.adsr~;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 151 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A classic ADSR envelope generator with four stages:
Attack (rise from 0 to 1) \, Decay (fall from 1 to the sustain level)
\, Sustain (hold at the sustain level while the gate is on) \, and
Release (fall back to 0 after the gate is turned off). The envelope
multiplies the incoming audio signal by its current value \, so it
is normally used as an amplitude envelope for oscillators \, samples
or other sound sources.;
